  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Recent civil unrest in Indonesia includes two distinct incidents: mass protests in Yogyakarta and a fatal dispute in Pati. In Yogyakarta, large-scale demonstrations at the local legislative building led to 154 arrests after events turned chaotic. The situation prompted visits from national-level officials to evaluate the aftermath. Simultaneously, a separate investigation is underway in Pati, where the village head of Sukoharjo, identified as Suparjo, died following a confrontation with a member of the local legislative council. Police reports indicate the conflict occurred during a mediation session regarding a debt dispute. Law enforcement officials have announced plans to question the legislative member involved, alongside two colleagues who were present during the encounter. These events have drawn attention to issues of public security and the conduct of legislative officials in local government settings.",
